---
title: "Native iMessage message metadata"
sidebarTitle: "Message metadata"
description: "Read curated Apple delivery, formatting, attachment, and reaction fields."
---

Cloud iMessage messages include a curated set of native metadata in addition
to Spectrum's cross-platform fields. The same fields are available on ordinary
inbound messages, messages returned by `space.getMessage()`, and native
outbound results. Synthetic events such as read receipts and group changes may
omit them.

When a streamed text send requires native edits, its returned record exposes
the final `nativeText` but omits the first-send metadata snapshot because those
lifecycle and formatting values no longer describe the edited message. Use
`space.getMessage()` when you need the current native state afterward.

| Use case | Fields |
|---|---|
| Delivery and lifecycle | `isSent`, `isDelivered`, `isDeliveredQuietly`, `didNotifyRecipient`, `isDelayed`, `sendErrorCode`, and the `dateDelivered`, `dateRead`, `datePlayed`, `dateEdited`, `dateRetracted`, and `dateExpressiveSendPlayed` timestamps |
| Native text | `nativeText`, `formatting`, `mentions`, `subject`, `balloonBundleId`, and `expressiveSendStyleId` |
| Attachments | `attachmentMetadata`, including transfer state, UTI, sticker/hidden status, original GUID, and Live Photo companion kind |
| Reactions and stickers | `appliedReactions`, `placedStickers`, and `reactionRecord` when the native row is itself a tapback |
| Classification | `itemType`, `groupTitle`, `partCount`, `isAutoReply`, `isCorrupt`, `isExpirable`, `isServiceMessage`, `isSpam`, and `isSystemMessage` |

Use `imessage.is()` when consuming the unified Spectrum message stream. It
narrows the message to the iMessage-specific type:

```ts
import { imessage } from "spectrum-ts/providers/imessage";

const message = await space.getMessage(messageId);

if (message && imessage.is(message)) {
  if ((message.sendErrorCode ?? 0) !== 0) {
    console.error("Apple send error", message.sendErrorCode);
  }

  console.log({
    sent: message.isSent,
    delivered: message.isDelivered,
    deliveredAt: message.dateDelivered,
    readAt: message.dateRead,
    editedAt: message.dateEdited,
    retractedAt: message.dateRetracted,
  });
}
```

The same guard works inside `for await (const [, message] of
spectrum.messages)`.

`nativeText` preserves Apple's original text because formatting and mention
ranges use UTF-16 offsets into that string. Spectrum can split native
multipart content into grouped messages, so rebuilding these offsets from
`message.content` is not reliable:

```ts
if (message && imessage.is(message)) {
  const text = message.nativeText;

  for (const mention of message.mentions ?? []) {
    console.log({
      address: mention.address,
      value: text?.slice(mention.start, mention.start + mention.length),
    });
  }
}
```

Attachment metadata describes Apple's transfer record; attachment bytes still
live in Spectrum attachment content:

```ts
if (message && imessage.is(message)) {
  for (const attachment of message.attachmentMetadata ?? []) {
    if (attachment.transferState === "failed") {
      console.error(`Attachment ${attachment.guid} failed to transfer`);
    }
  }

  for (const applied of message.appliedReactions ?? []) {
    console.log(applied.sender?.address, applied.reaction.kind);
  }
}
```

`sendErrorCode === 0` means Apple recorded no send error. The metadata is
intentionally curated: Spectrum does not expose the raw Advanced iMessage
database row or unstable Apple-private fields.

## Fresh upstream reads

Use `getMessageFresh` on the narrowed platform instance when a read must
observe the current upstream message and access state. Every call fetches the
message from Advanced iMessage through the client that serves `space.phone`;
it never returns a message from Spectrum's local cache.

```ts
const im = imessage(app);

if (typeof im.getMessageFresh !== "function") {
  // Older SDK: fresh reads are unavailable. Do not fall back to a cached read.
  throw new Error("iMessage fresh message reads are not supported");
}

const record = await im.getMessageFresh(space, messageId);
```

- **Returns** the raw iMessage provider record (`id`, `content`, `sender`,
  `space`, `timestamp`, and the native metadata fields above), not a wrapped
  Spectrum `Message`. Use `space.getMessage(messageId)` for the wrapped form.
  Both calls use the same provider function, so they behave identically.
- **Resolves `undefined`** when the upstream service reports that the message
  or multipart child is not found or hidden.
- **Rejects** on other upstream errors, such as revoked authentication or an
  unavailable access check. A rejection never falls back to cached content.
- **Older SDKs do not provide it.** Releases before `getMessageFresh` could
  serve `space.getMessage()` from a local cache, and `im.getMessageFresh` is
  `undefined` there. Unlike `getMessage`, it is not stubbed with an
  `UnsupportedError`, so checking for the method is a reliable capability
  test.

`getMessageFresh` requires `@spectrum-ts/imessage`. `@spectrum-ts/imessage-local`
does not provide it.

## Related content in streams

Some inbound stream events embed content they do not own: a reply carries
the message it quotes, a tapback or read receipt carries its target, and a
poll vote carries the poll's title and options. Spectrum fetches that related
content from Advanced iMessage every time it maps the event (`messages.get`
for messages, `polls.get` for polls). Its local caches can store the fresh
result, but they never decide whether related content is visible.

| Upstream lookup result | Reply (`message.received`) | Tapback, read receipt, poll vote |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Allowed | Embeds the current target | Emits with the current target or poll |
| Definitive (non-retryable) not found, hidden, or permission denied | Embeds a content-free stub target | Drops the event, and the stream cursor moves past it |
| Any retryable error, including a retryable not found or permission denied | Withholds the event, then retries it | Withholds the event, then retries it |
| Any other failure, such as an expired token or a non-retryable transport error | Withholds the event, then retries it | Withholds the event, then retries it |

A retried event is redelivered from the durable catch-up log. The stream
cursor does not advance past it, so the event arrives once, late, and not
with stale content. Until the lookup succeeds, later events on the same line
wait behind it. A request upstream rejects as malformed (`INVALID_ARGUMENT`)
is the one exception: it is skipped like any other unmappable event.

`space.getMessage()` and `getMessageFresh` resolve reply targets the same way.
When the reply target's access cannot be determined, they reject rather than
returning a stub target. Older SDKs returned a stub in this case.

These lookups cost one upstream read per event, so each reader's receipt
on the same message triggers its own read.
